/**
 * @defgroup solid_liquid_flue_gas_material_data_database Solid/Liquid Flue Gas Material Database
 * @ingroup databases
 * @brief Contains default data for solid/liquid flue gas materials used in process heat calculations.
 * @details This database provides default values for the composition and properties of common solid and liquid fuel flue gas materials. The data is used in process heat and combustion calculations for engineering analysis.
 *
 * @heading{Default Solid/Liquid Flue Gas Material Data}
 * @copydoc solid_liquid_flue_gas_material_data
 */

/**
 * @defgroup solid_liquid_flue_gas_material_data Default Solid/Liquid Flue Gas Material Data
 * @ingroup solid_liquid_flue_gas_material_data_database
 * The following table lists the default substances and their properties:
 *
 * | Substance                    | Carbon (%) | Hydrogen (%) | Sulfur (%) | Oxygen (%) | Nitrogen (%) | Moisture (%) | Ash (%) |
 * |------------------------------|------------|--------------|------------|------------|--------------|--------------|---------|
 * | Typical Bituminous Coal - US | 70.3       | 4.9          | 2.2        | 8.7        | 7.5          | 4.9          | 1.5     |
 * | Typical Anthracite - US      | 77.7       | 1.8          | 0.7        | 9.8        | 2.1          | 7.1          | 0.8     |
 * | Typical Lignite - US         | 47.5       | 3.4          | 0.8        | 8.3        | 14.2         | 25           | 0.8     |
 * | Fuel Oil #2                  | 86.6       | 12.8         | 0.5        | 0          | 0            | 0            | 0.1     |
 * | Fuel Oil #6                  | 87.1       | 10.6         | 2.1        | 0.2        | 0            | 0            | 0       |
 * | Typical Wood                 | 51.7       | 5.4          | 0.1        | 3.1        | 39.5         | 0            | 0.2     |
 *
 * @note Values are representative and may vary with source and measurement conditions.
 *
 * @see solid_liquid_flue_gas_material_calculator
 */
